        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(docs): reorder AGENTS.md template to protect critical rules from truncation (fixes #75187)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen workspace context is trimmed, safety-critical sections were positioned after Memory content and could be truncated out. Move Red Lines, External vs Internal, and Existing Solutions Preflight to the top — before First Run — so they survive context trimming.\n\nFixes #75187.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe three safety sections now appear right after the intro paragraph. Existing Solutions Preflight is restored (was accidentally dropped in the original reorder). All three are preserved.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNewly seeded workspaces always include safety guardrails regardless of context budget.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `docs/reference/templates/AGENTS.md` — 3 sections moved to top, all preserved\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD --check` — clean",
